# ADR 0001: Record architecture decisions

## Status

Accepted

## Context

We need a lightweight way to record significant structural and
architectural decisions for {{LibraryName}} so future contributors (human
or agent) understand *why* the repo looks the way it does, not just *what*
it looks like.

## Decision

We will use Architecture Decision Records (ADRs), one Markdown file per
decision, numbered sequentially, stored in `docs/design/adr/`. Each ADR
states the status, context, decision, and consequences.

## Consequences

Non-obvious structural choices (e.g. why smoke tests consume a packed
`.nupkg` instead of a project reference, why `src/` and `smoketests/` are
lowercase while project folders are PascalCase) get recorded here instead
of being re-litigated or silently "fixed" by someone who doesn't know the
reasoning.
